      "body": "Fixes #61389\n\n## What the issue was\nOn the prefill (producer) side, a request with `do_remote_decode=True` and `max_tokens=1` that samples EOS or a stop token as its first token finishes with `FINISHED_STOPPED`. MoRIIO ignored this status, so the prefill KV blocks were never exported and the decode side got no remote block metadata.\n\n## Why it happened\n`MoRIIOConnectorScheduler.request_finished()` in `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/moriio/moriio_connector.py` only continued when `request.status == FINISHED_LENGTH_CAPPED`. `check_stop()` sets `FINISHED_STOPPED` before the length cap is checked, so the method returned `(False, None)` early. The NIXL connector (`nixl/pull_scheduler.py`) already accepts both statuses.\n\n## The fix\nAccept `FINISHED_LENGTH_CAPPED` and `FINISHED_STOPPED`. Other statuses (e.g. aborted) still return early. Two files, 46 insertions, 3 deletions.\n\n## Not covered\nNo end-to-end test with a real MoRIIO P/D deployment (needs ROCm hardware). I did not audit other MoRIIO paths for similar status assumptions.\n\n## Validation\nRun:\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` on both changed files: pass.\n- `python -m py_compile` on both files, `git diff --check`: pass.\n- An isolated harness that executes the actual `request_finished` method body (extracted from the source) with stubbed dependencies, before and after the change. Before: `FINISHED_STOPPED` returned `delay_free=False, params=None`. After: `delay_free=True`, params with `remote_block_ids` returned, request tracked for deferred send. `FINISHED_LENGTH_CAPPED` unchanged; `FINISHED_ABORTED` still returns `(False, None)`.\n\nNot run: the new pytest tests (`tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_moriio_routing.py`). torch is not installable in my environment, and the module imports vLLM. Please run them locally; the stop-status case should fail without the source change and pass with it.\n\n## Steps to test\n```\ngit fetch https://github.com/Hmache/vllm fix/moriio-finished-stopped-remote-decode\ngit checkout FETCH_HEAD\npytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_moriio_routing.py -v\n# to confirm the regression test fails without the fix:\ngit checkout HEAD~1 -- vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/moriio/moriio_connector.py\npytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_moriio_routing.py -v\n```\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare this change; I reviewed it.",
